    <h2>Rachel</h2>
    <p>Rachel is the love of my life. I want to make her life the easiest it can possibly be, and the happiest it can possibly be.</p>
    <embed src="https://media.giphy.com/media/v1.Y2lkPWVjZjA1ZTQ3NmF1NGUyazR6N3pzcTY4dnh4N2x2Y3h6NTM2YzhkdmdsZzE4YzBjbCZlcD12MV9naWZzX3NlYXJjaCZjdD1n/7DRPFO0jRlxHTY2PIG/giphy.gif">
    <p>Its no secret that coding can unlock a multitude of chances to make great money, and i know she works two jobs, and is very stressed and tired especially when she has to go to both in the same day.</p>
    <p>Since I was a child i had always wanted to be a provider and protector of my family, so seeing her work so hard and we still are not where we want to be kills my heart.</p>
    <p>The choice i made was not only because of the stress she has, but I want us to have fun while we are still young too. I want to be able to travel the world, take cruises, and take her on shopping trips where she doesn't have to worry about a price.</p>
    <p>But biggest of all we both made an agreement to each other and ourselves that we would not bring a child into this world without first being married, and also having the freedom and resources for our child to not have to grow up poor. I made a promise with myself when i was 13 that I would never make my child go through the things i went through growing up poor.</p>
    <br>
    <h2>Kids</h2>
    <p>Kids are probably my biggest motivator for coding. I want to make enough money and still take care of my kids.</p>
    <embed src="https://media.giphy.com/media/v1.Y2lkPTc5MGI3NjExcnp2djJyZXNzMzg0ZDE0ZmpqMnVubTZjdGVhcDc3cWgxZjhrZGgzMyZlcD12MV9naWZzX3NlYXJjaCZjdD1n/5h2Kg1x9BGb2VorsFf/giphy.gif">
    <p>I never wanted to lack in both for instance. I know some children have present fathers, but they are poor and they are living in poverty or close to it. On the other hand some children have all the money in the world and lack a father to be there for them. Coding gives me the chance to do both. If i can land a career in web developlment or full stack development, I would be able to work from home being a present father, and make enough money for the lifestyle I want to live.</p>
    <p>The average pay for entry level web developers in MS is $41k–$65k, with top earners making $90k–$125k+.</p>
    <p>The average pay for entry level full stack developers in MS is $55k–$75k, with top earners making $100k–$130k+.</p>
    <p> That doesnt even count the fact that i can get hired for higer paying state while staying in MS and working online. This would allow me to live in MS (the lowest cost of living) but earn the pay rate of Cali(one of if not the highest cost of living states.) of course this would be once im much further down the road but its an important thing to remember.</p>
