    <h2>Purpose</h2>
    <p>Growing up i was very depressed and to be quite frank. I had planned on killing myself before I turned 21. I felt like there was no point to life, that i was born a failure, from a failure, and that nothing i ever did would ever work for me. I attempted to take my own life multiple times failing every time, from not festering up the courage to not cutting deep enough, to throwing up what i tied to poision myself with. When my mother passed I tried to drink her big bottle of Barnetts vodka and give myself alcohol posioning, but instead it just made me feel terrible the next day and throw up too much for my comfort. One thing it also did was a decison that would change my life for the better, an act i feel was a gift from God. I was uber confident now that i had lost soo much weight, and had filled my body with liquid confidence that I created a dating profile, just to see if I was the same undersiable guy I was before. This eventually led me to metting my soulmate Rachel. She doesn't know it but she saved my life.</p>
    <p>I say all of that to say for the first time in my 21 years of living I think i found my purpose. I have always grown up a gamer. I love all games from all consoles and genres, I can play it all. I also loved writing and creating. Ive falling in love with the idea of making my own games and websites. I truthfully feel like I have so many ideas for games and apps that can become big hits. I think i understand the market being a gamer myself, andi i understand what people want and dont want. I would share my game ideas with people and my eyes would sparkle. I think this is my passion and is what my purpose in the world is.</p>
